From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:53:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 30/34] coherent: exact late copies beside held writers, copy
 back before late batches

Path 4 (late_copy_in) took a write through another import only once its
writer's last batch was planned. A writer that signals after the write and
then waits for another event left its write out though Metal orders it
before the reader (late_beside_unplanned in census-r1). Each kept write now
carries the end of the parts it lies in, set as its encoder's parts are
recorded; the scheduler notes the parts planned per command buffer, and the
copy takes the write once its parts are planned. Writes left are counted by
why: late_beside_held (part held: Metal orders it after), _uncommitted, and
late_beside_unplanned now only for writes not known (ring of 256, joined
per open encoder).

A batch planned after its commit (it waited for a shared event) that meets
a trapping surface's bytes now syncs what completed since the commit's copy
back on the CPU, and records a copy back of what runs, planned, at its
start (Coherent::before_late_batch, counted plan_syncs/plan_copies_back/
plan_left). Before, the commit's copy back held back the reader's record
and the writer's later write was lost under the record's copy back.

Lanes: held_writer x3, late batch copy back; surface+event 168 passed, 1
known failure (ycbcr_textures), as at base.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
